&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring an Experiential Marketing Associate to join the Marketing team and help bring Coinbase to life through high-impact events and experiences. This team plans and executes events that drive brand awareness, deepen customer relationships, and support business goals across Consumer and Institutional audiences. You&#39;ll own the full lifecycle of event execution, from concept through post-event reporting, and coordinate across internal teams and external vendors to deliver polished, on-brand experiences that connect Coinbase with customers, partners, and the broader crypto community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end event execution across Coinbase&#39;s experiential marketing calendar, managing logistics including venue sourcing, vendor coordination, contract negotiation, budgets, and attendee management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with internal stakeholders across Marketing, Sales, Product, and Communications to align event programming with business priorities and ensure seamless delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain event project plans, timelines, and run-of-show documents, tracking all milestones from pre-event planning through post-event wrap-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support creative development for event experiences, collaborating with design and brand teams on invitations, signage, branded materials, and on-site activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track event budgets, manage vendor invoices, and reconcile expenses to ensure programs are delivered within approved spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure event performance by compiling post-event reports with attendance data, engagement metrics, and attribution to pipeline or revenue goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in event management or experiential marketing, with demonstrated ownership of end-to-end event logistics and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple events simultaneously, maintaining quality and meeting deadlines across overlapping timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with vendor and venue management, including contract negotiation and budget tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with event management platforms (e.g., Splash, Eventbrite, Cvent) and project management tools (e.g., Asana, Monday.com).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of compiling post-event reporting with measurable outcomes such as attendance targets, engagement rates, or attribution to leads and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
